features/ledger-economy-fixes/decisions.md:10:- Grant keys are bounded by what the ledger knows (islands; supply-cache ids given at creation), so a careless caller can't mint.
features/ledger-economy-fixes/decisions.md:15:  - Ruin keys are `String(island)`, and supply-cache ids live in the state.
features/ledger-economy-fixes/ledger-task.md:34:   - A `supply-cache` grant's key must be one of the supply-cache ids given at ledger creation (a new optional `supplyCaches` list in `createLedger`; none means no supply-cache grants). The list is stored in `LedgerState`, so `hashState` covers it, and `checkLedger` rejects any recorded grant whose key isn't a known island or supply cache.
docs/objectives.md:44:  - `tonics` (0–2) and `tonicEffect` (the last activation's `startTick` and `endTick`, or null).
docs/objectives.md:49:- `goldSpent`, `supplyCaches` (the supply-cache ids given to `createLedger`), `grants` and `requests`: see Economy.
docs/objectives.md:114:[Omitted long matching line]
features/ledger-economy/decisions.md:16:- Shops and supply-cache locations and interaction times are the caller's (world wiring) concern.
features/ledger-economy/ledger-task.md:27:- **Minted gold.** `grantGold(state, { playerId, reason, sourceKey, tick })`, with `reason` either `ruin` (40 gold) or `supply-cache` (25 gold); the amounts come from content.
features/ledger-economy/ledger-task.md:29:  - It is idempotent by its key: a `ruin` grant is once per (player, `sourceKey`), where the ruin id is the key; a `supply-cache` grant is once per `sourceKey` for the whole match (one global claim, §11).
